# SCALE LOCK (Setup's SEL list, LOOM-8; proj.rsv[3] SCALE_LOCK, the FM-1's setting): a synth track's note from the
# keys or from MIDI in snaps to the conductor's key and scale (a new project: C major) before it is played, written
# or remembered. Off (the default) a note is written as played; on, C# -> C (a tie goes down), F# -> F from MIDI in,
# and a note in the scale stays. Step record (REC tapped while stopped) shows what was written.
wait 300
# (WARP-8: a new project is eight kits; this scenario's melodic tracks are sample tracks)
knob 2 engine 6
knob 3 engine 6
knob 4 engine 6
knob 5 engine 6
knob 6 engine 6
knob 7 engine 6
knob 8 engine 6
wait 40
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
tap REC
wait 60
# off: C# (key 8: the keys start at F3, key 0) is written as it is
key 8 down
wait 30
key 8 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 1 61
tap REC
wait 60
# Setup > SEL > SCALE LOCK on
tap GLO
turn SELECT 5
expect page Setup
tap SEL
row SCALE LOCK
turn ALGO 1
tap HOME
wait 60
expect trk 2
tap REC
wait 60
# the cursor goes on after the step written: C# snaps to C
key 8 down
wait 30
key 8 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 2 60
# E (key 11) is in the scale
key 11 down
wait 30
key 11 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 3 64
# F# over MIDI on channel 2 snaps to F; its off (the same raw note) lets the step go and moves on
midi 91 42 64
wait 20
midi 81 42 40
wait 60
expect note 2 1 4 65
# a chord held: D#, G, B -> D, G, B
key 10 down
key 14 down
key 18 down
wait 30
key 10 up
key 14 up
key 18 up
wait 60
expect note 2 1 5 62
expect noteat 2 1 5 2 67
expect noteat 2 1 5 3 71
tap REC
wait 60
